libbb: a locked password never matches

su against a locked account ("!" or "*" in /etc/shadow, as root is until
root_password= is applied, #37) died in pw_encrypt() with "bad salt" and
skipped the failure log and delay.  Treat a locked hash as a wrong
password, so su logs the attempt, waits and prints "incorrect password".

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/libbb/correct_password.c
+++ b/libbb/correct_password.c
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@
 	if (!pw_pass[0]) { /* empty password field? */
 		return CHECKPASS_PW_HAS_EMPTY_PASSWORD;
 	}
+	/* A locked account never matches; pw_encrypt() would die on the
+	 * salt "!" or "*". */
+	if (pw_pass[0] == '!' || pw_pass[0] == '*')
+		return 0;
 
 	encrypted = pw_encrypt(plaintext, /*salt:*/ pw_pass, 1);
 	r = (strcmp(encrypted, pw_pass) == 0);
